{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$U = \\bigcup_{i \\in I} U_i$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-sheaf-axiom}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-definition-representable-by-open-immersions}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ada915862b08239daef876723fec155fbff656c832a2d772b7aec53e94c5edb2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8e0bfa4437d784b85562ffd6ada6fc776da7fba6fec9af497ba01db2aeb15bca", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe similarly say that <MATH_0001>\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>satisfies the sheaf property for the Zariski topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for\nevery open covering <MATH_0002> the diagram\n(<REF_0001>) is an equalizer diagram. See\nSchemes, Definition <REF_0002>.\nClearly, this is equivalent to saying that for every scheme <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004> the\nrestriction of <MATH_0005> to the opens of <MATH_0006> is a (usual) sheaf.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a4b271d28e43a422b2a2d0c71009e685d6360e1f1c675080ea563add7c69a6d5", "unit_id": "tag:03NV:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch/S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}(\\Spec(A)) \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}(\\Spec(B)) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}(\\Spec(B \\otimes_A B))\n}\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fpqc-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4f00c4bb8687d4cdcacbb8fdd9c7ca434a86dadfdc263beebc70891d7dabb7bd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2ddaa738ad0791efa994b9ad16cc898fa269bf332a323a1828f3f488fba1ad4d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a presheaf on <MATH_0002>. Then\n<MATH_0003> satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology\nif and only if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> satisfies the sheaf property with respect to the\nZariski topology, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every faithfully flat morphism <MATH_0005>\nof affine schemes over <MATH_0006>, the sheaf axiom holds for the covering\n<MATH_0007>. Namely, this means that\n<MATH_0008>\nis an equalizer diagram.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f2c68669070b9ac773cb844c32bc326315e8d55b8ebbff7d2bd8d32b3327b271", "unit_id": "tag:03O1:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-sheaf-property-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:97b65c65e0b0e9d50131025a46d737000b2701fb3be57ab3222752cd7014da8d", "source_text": "See Topologies, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf46abbdb3c1a0c9e7cd6f1379076750d3d7d04a5edbad791b6deae82fbf75db", "unit_id": "tag:03O1:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"ITEMCLOSE_0001": "]", "ITEMCLOSE_0002": "]", "ITEMCLOSE_0003": "]", "ITEMOPEN_0001": "\\item[", "ITEMOPEN_0002": "\\item[", "ITEMOPEN_0003": "\\item[", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch/S$", "MATH_0003": "$T/S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}_T$", "MATH_0005": "$T_{Zar}$", "MATH_0006": "$f : T' \\to T$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}_T \\to \\mathcal{F}_{T'}$", "MATH_0009": "$f : T' \\to T$", "MATH_0010": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}_T \\to \\mathcal{F}_{T'}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}_{\\Spec(A)}(\\Spec(A)) \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}_{\\Spec(B)}(\\Spec(B)) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}_{\\Spec(B \\otimes_A B)}(\\Spec(B \\otimes_A B))\n}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$\\Sch/S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fpqc-sheaves}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1d7c7d1b31b508dcd5bde44eb94f82397fd9720919b404b8ea7537bef8db2d22", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8fb541e8d37811f05deec5e2e9bcad20979fa5c8a18d5de72ac30f9137f69fcb", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAn alternative way to think of a presheaf <MATH_0001> on\n<MATH_0002> which satisfies the sheaf condition for the\nfpqc topology is as the following data:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> for each <MATH_0003>, a usual (i.e., Zariski) sheaf <MATH_0004> on\n<MATH_0005>,\n<STRUCT_0004> for every map <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>, a restriction mapping\n<MATH_0008>\n<STRUCT_0005>\nsuch that\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(a)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> the restriction mappings are functorial,\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(b)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0009> is an open immersion then the restriction\nmapping <MATH_0010> is an isomorphism, and\n<ITEMOPEN_0003>(c)<ITEMCLOSE_0003> for every faithfully flat morphism\n<MATH_0011> over <MATH_0012>, the diagram\n<MATH_0013>\nis an equalizer.\n<STRUCT_0007>\nData (1) and (2) and conditions (a), (b) give the data of a presheaf\non <MATH_0014> satisfying the sheaf condition for the Zariski topology.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001> condition (c) then suffices to get the\nsheaf condition for the fpqc topology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:42aa4797845586dcea757a2976c89a473499c4208aec5889f201a44d86ee74fb", "unit_id": "tag:03NV:prose-0004"}
